<% content_for :own_heading, true %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
  <%= render "admin/component_demo/environment_banner" %>

  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <% description = "Save grades and Finalize grades: why the page does not say you need both, and what " \
                   "to change." %>
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "Grade book actions", description: description } do %><% end %>

  <div class="space-y-10">
    <section data-testid="gb-today">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">What the page does today</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
        Measured on the real page: <strong>Save grades</strong> is a filled primary at 496px, on the page
        background under the table. <strong>Finalize grades</strong> is an outlined danger button at 757px,
        inside its own card. Neither mentions the other.
      </p>

      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
          <strong>Each is following a different rule, and both rules are right.</strong> design.md puts a
          <em>form's</em> actions on the leading edge below the card, on the page background - Save is the
          grades form's submit, so outside is correct. The finalize block is not a form card, it is a
          decision panel, and its button is that section's own action - so inside is correct too. Two
          correct rules, one page that reads as arbitrary.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">
          So the fix is not to move a button. It is that <strong>nothing on the page expresses the
          sequence</strong>, and one thing actively hides it.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="gb-hazard">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">The part that is not cosmetic</h2>
      <%= render "components/ui/callout",
                 tone: :warning,
                 title: "Finalize pays whatever is in the database, not what is on screen",
                 body: "The page autosaves every 30 seconds and on nothing else - not on blur, not on " \
                       "change. Type a grade and press Finalize inside that window and the old grade is " \
                       "what gets paid. Nothing on the page says so." %>

      <div class="mt-4">
        <%= render "components/ui/callout",
                   tone: :warning,
                   title: "And both buttons are autosave targets",
                   body: "The timer clicks buttonTarget, which is the first one in the DOM. That is " \
                         "Save today, purely because the finalize card renders after the table. Move " \
                         "the finalize card above the table and the autosave timer pays the students " \
                         "every 30 seconds." %>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="gb-option-a">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">A. Save on blur, and show it &mdash; recommended</h2>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <span class="tw-btn-primary">Save grades</span>
          <span class="text-sm text-slate-600">All changes saved &middot; 14:32</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">
          The window closes at the root: a field that loses focus is saved, so by the time a hand reaches
          Finalize there is nothing unsaved. The status line is what makes that believable - an app that
          saves silently and says nothing is one people press Save on twice.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="gb-option-b">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">B. Say what Finalize acts on &mdash; recommended</h2>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: { title: "Then finalize the quarter" } do %>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">
          Pays $12.40 into 2 students' portfolios and locks these entries. This cannot be undone.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">Uses your saved grades, above.</p>
        <div class="mt-5">
          <span class="tw-btn-danger-outline">Finalize grades</span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
        Two words of sequencing in the heading - <strong>"Then finalize the quarter"</strong> rather than
        "Finalize this quarter" - and one line saying what it reads. That is the whole of the clarity
        problem, and it costs nothing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="gb-option-c">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">C. Swap the emphasis</h2>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <span class="tw-btn-secondary">Save grades</span>
          <span class="tw-btn-primary">Finalize grades</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">
          <strong>Rejected.</strong> It reads as the obvious answer to "the important one should be
          primary", and it is backwards: on a page for entering grades the frequent action is saving, and
          the terminal one happens once per quarter. Making an irreversible payment the brightest thing on
          screen is the always-on alarm design.md rules out, and it invites the press it should discourage.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="gb-option-d">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">D. One action bar with both</h2>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <span class="text-sm text-slate-600">All changes saved &middot; 14:32</span>
          <span class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="tw-btn-secondary">Save grades</span>
            <span class="tw-btn-danger-outline">Finalize grades</span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">
          <strong>Rejected.</strong> Putting them side by side makes them look like alternatives - two ways
          to finish - when one is "keep working" and the other is "pay real money and lock the quarter".
          It also drops the earnings breakdown that sits above Finalize today, which is the only place the
          person authorising the payment sees what it is made of.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <section data-testid="gb-recommendation">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Recommendation</h2>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: {} do %>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
          <strong>A and B, plus the autosave fix.</strong> Keep both buttons where they are and keep the
          emphasis as it is - each is following a rule that holds. What is missing is sequence and
          certainty, and those are words and a save-on-blur, not a new layout:
        </p>
        <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-slate-700">
          <li>Save when a field loses focus, not only every 30 seconds, so nothing typed is ever unsaved
            by the time Finalize is reachable.</li>
          <li>Show the save state in words beside the Save button.</li>
          <li>Head the finalize card <strong>"Then finalize the quarter"</strong> and add
            <strong>"Uses your saved grades, above."</strong></li>
          <li>Take <code>autosave_target: "button"</code> off the finalize button, so the timer cannot
            ever click it, whatever order the page is rendered in.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">
          Item 4 is a defect fix rather than a design change, and I would do it whichever option you pick.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
